PROGRAM – 6

TITLE: Continuous Integration with Jenkins using Maven

AIM:
To set up a Continuous Integration (CI) pipeline in Jenkins and build a Maven project automatically.

PROCEDURE:

1. Open Jenkins Dashboard.

2. Click Manage Jenkins → Plugins.

3. Search and install Maven Integration Plugin.

4. Verify that Maven Project option is available.

5. Go to Manage Jenkins → Tools.

6. Configure Maven installation (MAVEN_HOME).

7. Click New Item.

8. Enter Project Name and select Freestyle Project.

9. Click OK.

10. Under Build section, click Add Build Step.

11. Select Invoke top-level Maven targets.

12. Choose the configured Maven version.

13. Enter Goal:

    clean install

14. In Advanced options, specify the path of pom.xml.

15. Click Apply and Save.

16. Click Build Now.

17. View the build result in Console Output.

COMMAND:

```text
clean install
```

OUTPUT:

```text
BUILD SUCCESS
```

RESULT:
Successfully configured a Jenkins CI Pipeline and built the Maven project using Jenkins.
